%% DM26-0670

%% From the repository set to the graph, as built (2026-11-04, docs/architecture/git-controller.md, protocol-handlers.md). How a proposal enters the set is
%% general/proposal_flow, how the credential gets there general/escrowed_credential_lifecycle, and the handler's judgment general/protocol_handler_request.
%% A push to Polar's git server, at the end, concerns only the scheduler observer: the git observer polls.
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Admin as Administrator
    participant Ctl as git-repo-controller
    participant Obs as git-repo-observer<br/>(a worker per repository)
    participant H as Protocol handler<br/>(in the observer)
    participant Site as The git host
    participant Proc as git-repo-processor
    participant Graph as Neo4j

    Admin->>Ctl: signed runtime section repositories, by delivery or replay
    Ctl->>Ctl: the set: the signed entries plus accepted proposals. A signed entry wins, and skips admission and the guard
    loop on a change, and every 60 s
        Ctl-)Obs: RepositorySet { repositories, complete } on git.repo.config.events, whole and unsigned
    end
    Note over Ctl,Obs: complete is false for its first 600 s, so a restarted controller's partial set stops nothing.<br/>When it is true, the observer stops what the set leaves out
    Obs->>Obs: reconcile: a worker for each repository

    loop at once, then every frequency seconds (900 by default)
        Obs->>H: git.fetch, a bound location with the chosen credential,<br/>or git.fetch-public, arbitrary and with no credential
        H->>H: judge it, a host that asked for time, a credential refused before
        opt git.fetch
            H->>H: the credential for this host, from the CryptoActor, which checks the binding
            Note over H: None registered: the worker reports pending-credential, and tries again when a version arrives
        end
        rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
        Note over H,Site: DESIGNED (git-controller.md, "The observer's own checks"), not built
        H->>H: at connect, refuse a private, loopback, link-local or cluster address, https only
        end
        H->>Site: bare clone or fetch, through the egress proxy, redirects refused
        Site-->>H: the objects
        H->>H: run the observer's read over the clone: the walk of each ref (plan_ref)
        H-->>Obs: the commits and tips, never the credential
        Obs-)Proc: CommitDiscovered batches, oldest first, then RefUpdated if the tip moved,<br/>on polar.git.repositories.events
        Obs-)Proc: ObservationStatus on polar.git.observation.status, for each attempt
        Proc->>Graph: GitRepository, GitCommit, CONTAINS, PARENT
        Proc->>Graph: GitRef POINTS_TO with observed_at, old edges kept, and status as properties
    end

    rect rgb(235, 219, 178)
    Note over Obs,Graph: DESIGNED (git-controller.md, "Status and checkpoints"), not built. Today what is walked is remembered<br/>in the worker's memory only, so a restarted observer walks again. The controller does not read the status yet
    Obs-)Proc: a starting observer asks, through the state agent, for the last tip of each ref
    Proc-->>Obs: the newest POINTS_TO
    end
